const cards = [
{id:'validation',title:'Backend Validation',zh:'后端校验 · Trust the rules, not the request.',tag:'API DESIGN',definition:'Validate incoming data on the server to protect data integrity and enforce business rules.',translation:'前端校验帮助用户正确填写；后端校验确保绕过页面的请求也必须遵守规则。类型正确，不代表业务有效。',example:'// quantity is already an integer. Is it valid?\nif (quantity <= 0)\n{\n    return Results.BadRequest("Quantity must be positive.");\n}',takeaway:'Type validation: Can it be parsed as an integer?\nBusiness validation: Is that integer allowed?',answer:'We need backend validation because clients can call the API directly and bypass frontend validation. The backend must validate incoming data to protect data integrity and enforce business rules.',question:'The frontend prevents negative quantities. Why must the API still reject quantity = -2?',solution:'A caller can bypass the UI. Subtracting -2 would increase stock by 2 and create an invalid order. Validate quantity > 0 before modifying data.'},
{id:'race',title:'Race Conditions',zh:'竞态条件 · When timing changes the outcome.',tag:'CONCURRENCY',definition:'A race condition occurs when the outcome depends on the timing of concurrent operations.',translation:'“先查询是否可用，再创建预订”是两个步骤。两个请求可能都在对方保存之前读到“可用”，从而重复预订。',example:'Request A → checks availability → Available\nRequest B → checks availability → Available\nRequest A → creates booking     → Success\nRequest B → creates booking     → Success\n\nResult: two overlapping bookings for one vehicle.',takeaway:'The availability check and booking creation are not atomic. A transaction alone does not automatically prevent this; the isolation and concurrency strategy matter.',answer:'Both requests may succeed because each request can check availability before the other saves its booking. This race condition can lead to double booking. We need database-enforced concurrency control.',question:'Does wrapping the availability check and INSERT in a transaction always prevent double booking? Explain.',solution:'No. For example, under read committed isolation, both transactions may observe no booking before either inserts. Use an appropriate strategy such as locking a shared vehicle row within the transaction, a supported database exclusion constraint, or serializable isolation with retry handling.'},
{id:'idempotency',title:'Idempotency',zh:'幂等性 · Retry safely, without duplicate effects.',tag:'API RELIABILITY',definition:'Repeating the same operation has the same intended effect as performing it once.',translation:'第一次请求可能已成功，但响应丢失。同一次预订的重试使用相同的幂等键，让服务端识别它，而不是再创建一笔。key 代表一次业务操作，不是一个用户。用户确认预订时生成并保存 key；超时、断网或处理中重复点击，沿用原 key 和参数。成功后点击“再订一笔”，或修改日期后重新确认，使用新 key。不能仅凭参数相同或时间接近判断用户意图。',example:'POST /api/bookings\nIdempotency-Key: booking-attempt-7f92\n\nFirst request → create booking → save key + result\nSame-key retry → return the existing result\nNew booking intention → use a new key\n\n// Create ONCE when confirming the operation:\nconst operation = { key: crypto.randomUUID(), payload };\n// Every send/retry uses operation.key + operation.payload.\n// Never generate a new key inside each network attempt.',takeaway:'Debouncing reduces repeated triggers. Idempotency prevents duplicate business effects. Different users with different keys still need concurrency control.\nKeep the pending operation key and payload; persist them to resume after refresh, or use a server-managed booking draft ID. A timeout means the outcome is unknown, not that creation failed.\nA new key does not cancel an unresolved original booking. Reconcile that booking before replacing it. Use a scoped unique key and coordinate the booking write and idempotency record atomically; check-then-insert alone races.',answer:'I generate a key once when the user confirms a booking operation. I keep that key and payload for retries, because a timeout may hide a successful booking. A new confirmed operation gets a new key, even if its parameters match. Request contents alone cannot tell us the user’s intent. The backend records the key and result, so a retry does not create another booking. A unique constraint helps coordinate concurrent requests with the same key.',question:'A booking times out, the user clicks Retry, then refreshes the page. Which key should be used? After success, they book the same dates again. Is that a retry? Do different users with different keys avoid double booking?',solution:'Retry uses the original key and payload. After refresh, restore the pending operation from storage or a server-managed draft. After success, explicitly booking again is a new operation with a new key, even with identical parameters. Disable repeat clicks while pending and retain the same key. Changing dates requires a new confirmed operation, but first reconcile the unresolved original: a new key does not cancel it. Different users with different keys are distinct operations. Idempotency protects retries of one operation. Availability requires separate concurrency control. Scope keys to the user or tenant, check payload consistency, and define how in-progress requests and key expiration are handled.'},
{id:'overlap',title:'Interval Overlap',zh:'区间重叠 · Availability lives on a timeline.',tag:'DATABASE LOGIC',definition:'Two half-open time intervals overlap when each interval starts before the other interval ends.',translation:'使用 [start, end)：包含开始时间，不包含结束时间。因此一位用户 10:00 还车，另一位可以 10:00 取车。实际业务可另外加入清洁缓冲时间。',example:'// Assume valid intervals: Start < End\nbool overlaps =\n    existing.Start < requested.End &&\n    requested.Start < existing.End;\n\nExisting: Nov 10, 10:00 → Nov 12, 10:00\nRequest:  Nov 12, 10:00 → Nov 14, 10:00\nResult:   no overlap',takeaway:'Define boundary semantics, valid date ranges, time zones, and which booking statuses block availability. An overlap query detects conflicts; it does not alone prevent concurrent inserts.',answer:'I use half-open intervals, where the start is included and the end is excluded. Two bookings overlap if each starts before the other ends. This allows back-to-back bookings, assuming no turnaround buffer is required.',question:'Existing: Nov 10 at 10:00 to Nov 12 at 10:00. Do Nov 11–13 and Nov 9–10 (all at 10:00) overlap?',solution:'Nov 11–13 overlaps. Nov 9–10 does not: it ends exactly when the existing booking begins. Validate Start < End, and use consistent instants when comparing timestamps.'}
];
cards.push(
{id:'interview-components',title:'Tell me about a reusable component you built.',zh:'组件设计 · 用真实经历解释复用与取舍',tag:'INTERVIEW · FRONTEND',definition:'Explain the repeated problem, your component boundary, its API, and the trade-offs.',translation:'结合华为项目中可复用组件的经历。先选一个你确实做过的组件，再补充输入、事件、状态归属和一个设计取舍。以下为基于简历的回答起点，不是完整的已核实故事。',example:'Problem → repeated behaviour\nYour role → what you designed or implemented\nAPI → props, events, slots / children\nDecision → shared behaviour versus page-specific logic\nEvidence → how you checked it worked',takeaway:'Follow-ups:\nWhat stayed outside the component?\nHow did you handle state and validation?\nWhen would you avoid reuse?\nHow would you implement it in React?\nDescribe your actual Vue work first; label React alternatives as a proposed approach.',answer:'On the Huawei client project, I worked with Vue 3 and TypeScript and built reusable components for enterprise interfaces. One component I can explain in detail is [a real component]. It addressed [a repeated problem]. I was responsible for [my part]. I kept [shared behaviour] inside and [page-specific logic] outside because [reason]. I checked it through [actual verification].',question:'Speak for 90 seconds about one real reusable component. Then explain one trade-off without reading your notes.',solution:'Use one specific example: problem → your contribution → component API → design choice → verification. Replace every bracket with a true detail. Explain what happened if reuse became too complicated. Do not invent component names, performance gains, or test coverage.'},
{id:'interview-integration',title:'What integration issue did you encounter?',zh:'接口联调 · 讲清证据与排查过程',tag:'INTERVIEW · DEBUGGING',definition:'Describe a real integration failure, how you narrowed down its cause, and how the fix was verified.',translation:'简历中有 Axios / REST API 集成，以及与后端和 QA 解决联调问题的经历。选一个记得细节的真实问题，不需要编造严重事故。',example:'Symptom → expected versus actual behaviour\nEvidence → request, response, UI state, reproduction\nCause → what the evidence established\nAction → your change and team coordination\nVerification → original case and related cases',takeaway:'Follow-ups:\nHow did you know where the bug was?\nWhat if the API returned 200 but the data was wrong?\nHow did you handle loading and error states?\nWhat would prevent the same issue?\nA suspected cause is not a confirmed cause.',answer:'I integrated REST APIs in my frontend roles and worked with backend developers and QA on integration issues. One example was [a real issue]. The expected behaviour was [expected], but we observed [actual]. I checked [evidence], which showed [cause]. My part in the fix was [action]. We verified it by [actual checks].',question:'Explain one real API integration issue in 90 seconds. Be ready to describe the request and response you inspected.',solution:'Include an observable symptom, the evidence that changed your understanding, your own action, and the verification. If a detail is uncertain, say so. Do not present a hypothetical API mismatch as an incident from your employment.'},
{id:'interview-ownership',title:'What did you personally own?',zh:'个人贡献 · 准确区分 I 与 we',tag:'INTERVIEW · OWNERSHIP',definition:'State your delivery boundary and distinguish your individual work from the team outcome.',translation:'从房产详情、视频看房、客户跟进、规则配置或报表界面中选一个你真正负责的功能。说明你实现了什么、依赖谁、遇到什么决策，以及谁负责后端和最终验收。',example:'Team goal → the feature and its users\nMy scope → implementation, decisions, checks\nDependencies → API, design, QA\nBoundary → what teammates owned\nOutcome → a result you can support',takeaway:'Follow-ups:\nWhich decision did you make yourself?\nWhat was the hardest part of your scope?\nWhat did someone else own?\nWhat would you do differently?\nUse I for your actions and we for shared outcomes. No invented metrics.',answer:'On [a real project], the team was building [feature]. I was responsible for [specific frontend scope], including [actual tasks]. I worked with [teammates] on [dependency], while they owned [their scope]. One decision I made was [decision] because [reason]. The result was [a supported outcome].',question:'Choose one feature from your CV. Explain your personal contribution in 60–90 seconds, then name the limits of your responsibility.',solution:'A strong answer makes your scope easy to identify: I implemented X; I coordinated Y; the backend developer owned Z. Include one decision and its reason. Avoid claiming sole ownership of a team project or describing personal practice as commercial backend experience.'},
{id:'interview-collaboration',title:'How did you work with the backend and QA teams?',zh:'团队协作 · 用一个具体问题说明沟通方式',tag:'INTERVIEW · COLLABORATION',definition:'Show how you aligned expectations, shared evidence, resolved a problem, and confirmed the result with teammates.',translation:'你有与产品、Java 后端和 QA 协作的经历。先简述协作方式，再用一次真实联调或缺陷处理说明如何推动事情完成。不要仅说“沟通很好”。',example:'Context → feature and shared expectations\nAlignment → API fields, validation, error behaviour\nIssue → reproduction and evidence\nResolution → agreed action and owners\nConfirmation → retest and acceptance',takeaway:'Follow-ups:\nWhat if you disagreed about expected behaviour?\nHow did you report a bug clearly?\nWhat did you do when the API was delayed?\nHow did you decide a fix was ready?\nOnly mention processes and tools you actually used.',answer:'On the Huawei client project, I worked with product, Java backend developers and QA to deliver frontend features. For [a real example], we needed to agree on [behaviour or API detail]. I shared [actual evidence or questions], and we agreed on [action]. I handled [my part], and [teammate] handled [their part]. We confirmed the result through [actual verification].',question:'Give a two-minute answer with one real collaboration example. Then answer: What did you do when expectations differed?',solution:'Describe a shared goal, a concrete communication action, the agreed resolution, and how completion was checked. For disagreement, explain how you clarified requirements with evidence and the relevant decision owner. Do not invent conflict, team ceremonies, or tools.'}
);
let state={current:'validation',statuses:{},notes:{},practice:false};let canSave=true;try{const saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('devnotes-v1')||'null');if(saved&&typeof saved==='object')state={...state,...saved,statuses:saved.statuses||{},notes:saved.notes||{}}}catch{}
let query='',revealed=false;const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);const escapeHTML=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));const list=()=>cards.filter(c=>(c.title+' '+c.zh+' '+c.tag+' '+c.definition).toLowerCase().includes(query));
function save(){try{localStorage.setItem('devnotes-v1',JSON.stringify(state))}catch{canSave=false;$('#saveStatus').textContent='Progress unavailable · browser storage blocked'}}
function go(id){state.current=id;revealed=false;save();render();$('#card').scrollTop=0}
function move(delta){const a=list(),i=a.findIndex(c=>c.id===state.current);if(a[i+delta])go(a[i+delta].id)}
function render(){const a=list();let c=a.find(c=>c.id===state.current);if(!c)c=a[0];if(c)state.current=c.id;const i=a.indexOf(c);$('#topics').innerHTML=a.length?a.map((x,n)=>`<button data-id="${x.id}" class="${x===c?'active':''}" ${x===c?'aria-current="page"':''}><span class="num">0${cards.indexOf(x)+1}</span>${x.title}<small>${state.statuses[x.id]==='Confident'?'✓':'↗'}</small></button>`).join(''):'<p class="empty">No matching concepts.</p>';$('#count').textContent=String(a.length).padStart(2,'0');$('#position').textContent=c?`${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / ${String(a.length).padStart(2,'0')} CONCEPTS`:'0 CONCEPTS';const done=cards.filter(x=>state.statuses[x.id]==='Confident').length;$('#percent').textContent=`${Math.round(done/cards.length*100)}%`;$('#progress').style.width=`${Math.round(done/cards.length*100)}%`;$('#mastered').textContent=`${done} of ${cards.length} cards marked confident`;$('#mode').classList.toggle('selected',state.practice);$('#mode').textContent=state.practice?'◎ Practice mode · ON':'◎ Practice mode';$('#mode').setAttribute('aria-pressed',state.practice);$('#prev').disabled=!c||i<=0;$('#next').disabled=!c||i>=a.length-1;if(!c){$('#card').innerHTML='<h2>No concepts found</h2><p>Try “API”, “race”, or “数据库”.</p>';return}
const learning=`<p class="definition">${c.definition}</p><p class="zh">${c.translation}</p><div class="label">IN THE CODE / IN THE REAL WORLD</div><pre>${escapeHTML(c.example)}</pre><div class="callout">${escapeHTML(c.takeaway).replace(/\n/g,'<br>')}</div><div class="rule"></div><div class="label">SAY IT IN YOUR INTERVIEW</div><div class="answer">“${c.answer}”</div>`;
$('#card').innerHTML=`<div class="card-top"><span class="tag">${c.tag}</span><span class="read-time">◷ 3 MIN READ</span></div><h2 class="title">${c.title}</h2><p class="subtitle">${c.zh}</p>${state.practice?'':learning}<section class="practice"><div class="label">YOUR TURN · ACTIVE RECALL</div><p>${c.question}</p><textarea id="note" aria-label="Your practice answer" placeholder="Explain it in your own words… English or 中文都可以。">${escapeHTML(state.notes[c.id]||'')}</textarea><button id="reveal" class="secondary" aria-expanded="${revealed}">${revealed?'Hide':'Reveal'} suggested answer ↓</button>${revealed?`<p class="answer">${c.solution}</p>${state.practice?learning:''}`:''}</section><div class="label">HOW WELL DO YOU KNOW THIS?</div><div class="statuses">${['Learning','Needs Review','Confident'].map((s,n)=>`<button data-status="${s}" aria-pressed="${(state.statuses[c.id]||'Learning')===s}" class="${(state.statuses[c.id]||'Learning')===s?'selected':''}">${['◔','↻','✓'][n]} ${s}</button>`).join('')}</div>`;
$('#note').addEventListener('input',e=>{state.notes[c.id]=e.target.value;save()});$('#reveal').onclick=()=>{const top=$('#card').scrollTop;revealed=!revealed;render();$('#card').scrollTop=top};document.querySelectorAll('[data-status]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{const top=$('#card').scrollTop;state.statuses[c.id]=b.dataset.status;save();render();$('#card').scrollTop=top});document.querySelectorAll('[data-id]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>go(b.dataset.id));}
$('#prev').onclick=()=>move(-1);$('#next').onclick=()=>move(1);$('#mode').onclick=()=>{state.practice=!state.practice;revealed=false;save();render();$('#card').scrollTop=0};$('#search').oninput=e=>{query=e.target.value.toLowerCase().trim();revealed=false;render();save();$('#card').scrollTop=0};document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(/INPUT|TEXTAREA|SELECT/.test(e.target.tagName)||e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey||e.altKey)return;if(e.key==='ArrowRight'||e.key==='ArrowLeft'){e.preventDefault();move(e.key==='ArrowRight'?1:-1)}});
let lastWheel=0,edgeDirection=0,edgeSince=0,wheelSum=0;$('#card').addEventListener('wheel',e=>{if(e.ctrlKey||Math.abs(e.deltaX)>Math.abs(e.deltaY)||e.target.closest('textarea'))return;const el=$('#card'),now=Date.now(),dir=Math.sign(e.deltaY);if(!dir)return;const edge=dir>0?el.scrollTop+el.clientHeight>=el.scrollHeight-3:el.scrollTop<=2;if(!edge){edgeDirection=0;wheelSum=0;return}e.preventDefault();if(now-lastWheel<850)return;if(edgeDirection!==dir||now-edgeSince>450){edgeDirection=dir;edgeSince=now;wheelSum=0}wheelSum+=Math.abs(e.deltaY)*(e.deltaMode===1?16:e.deltaMode===2?el.clientHeight:1);if(now-edgeSince<160||wheelSum<70)return;move(dir);lastWheel=now;edgeDirection=0;wheelSum=0},{passive:false});render();save();
